{
  "//": "Which recipes are a step on the way rather than a thing to have. The crafting screen hides each list behind a checkbox (both on by default). Ids only; nothing here is CDDA text.",
  "rules": {
    "component": "The result is only ever a step on the way: it feeds other recipes and cannot be worn, eaten, read or held as a tool on its own. A refined material made from a raw one (a plank from a log, thread from fibre, steel from scrap) is a component. Anything with a tool quality, anything wearable and anything a survivor would pick up to use is not.",
    "modification": "One finished thing re-cut or re-fitted into a variant of itself: sleeves off, fingers off, cropped, ripped, shortened, padded, studded, armoured or reinforced. Cooking, drying, threshing and milling are the food chain, not modifications, and assembling a suit out of its pieces is a making of its own.",
    "review": "Both lists are hand-reviewed. A new entry has to be an id the loader knows (scripts/validate-data.mjs checks that) and has to pass the two rules above."
  },
